# Zig build-system cache: build graph, compiler intermediates, codegen
# scratch. Everything in here is content-hash keyed and fully regenerated
# by `zig build`, so it is never worth committing.
.zig-cache/
zig-cache/

# Install prefix written by `zig build` / `zig build install`
# (zig-out/bin/rticz, zig-out/bin/rticz-cli). Regenerate instead of commit.
zig-out/

# Local package cache populated by `zig fetch` (older workflow; harmless
# to keep listed for projects that grow dependencies).
.deps/

# Codegen lives in src/generated/: the generators, the stubs they
# compile against, and the modules they emit — nothing codegen-related
# outside this folder.  The tools and stubs are committed (they are
# hand-written); only what the build *emits* is ignored: `zig build`
# rewrites these files on every run, so committing them would only
# invite stale copies.  They are placed in the source tree, not the
# build cache, so the emitted table and contexts are readable as-is.
src/generated/irq.zig
src/generated/context.zig

# Editor / OS cruft.
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
